  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1235 AM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nA weak upper level ridge will be over south-central and southeast \nTexas Tuesday. With lower heights over our area and moist air, \nisolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms will be possible \nTuesday. The ridge will strengthen some over southeast Texas \nWednesday and Thursday, and then shift back to the west over Deep \nSouth Texas by next weekend. Temperatures Tuesday and Wednesday \nwill be slightly cooler but still above normal (highs mostly in \nthe lower 90s). Expect a trend toward hotter temperatures again by\nthe weekend with highs in the lower and mid 90s. While the \npossibility of an isolated shower/thunderstorm cannot be ruled \nout, overall rain chances dwindle for our area in the mid-to-late \nweek time frame and into the weekend. Medium range models have \nincreased differences in the upper level pattern and surface \nfeatures Sunday into the first part of next week and this has\nimplications on rain chances and temperatures. For this part of\nthe forecast, relying more on the model blends.",
